      "id": 1,
      "text": "Middleburgh’s name traces back to Middelburg, the Dutch Republic’s capital in Zeeland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middleburgh_(village)%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1712, Middleburgh grew from a Palatine settlement by Johan Conrad Weiser into a thriving village in Schoharie Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wwhitmanbooks.com/about-middleburgh",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Middleburgh‑Schoharie Railroad, half‑based in the village, sparked a boom along Railroad Avenue before ceasing operations in 1936.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middleburgh_(village)%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2011, Hurricane Irene devastated Middleburgh, leaving lasting damage that reshaped the village’s landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middleburgh_(village)%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The current Middleburgh Public Library sits where the historic Dock once stood, a site that later housed a gas station.",
